From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fingerprint Lab <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 16:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] goodix550c: stop sleeping the sensor between enrollment stages

The blackout follows an action that ends in sleep, and the enrollment loop ends
every single stage that way: the finger-up wait it runs between stages closes
with GOODIX_FINGER_UP_SLEEP, and the next stage reads its reference frame
350ms later. The trigger therefore fires once per stage rather than once per
action.

The measurements match. A three-finger session logged 25 empty reference
frames across its stages, and the operator independently noticed that pausing
before re-placing a finger made stages register, which is what waiting out the
recovery looks like from the outside.

Between stages the sleep buys nothing, because another capture follows at once.
Keep it for the last stage, where the action really is ending, and for
verification, which does finish there. The flag is consumed by the wait that
reads it so it cannot leak into a later action.

This removes the trigger from the enrollment path rather than absorbing it.
Why the sensor stops answering after a sleep is still unknown, and the retry
budget from the previous patch still covers the cases that remain.

---

--- a/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-enroll.c
+++ b/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-enroll.c
@@ -157,6 +157,13 @@
       break;
 
     case GOODIX_ENROLL_WAIT_FINGER_UP:
+      /* The finger-up wait ends by putting the sensor to sleep, and this sensor
+       * stops answering image requests for seconds afterwards: an enrolment
+       * measured 25 empty reference frames across its stages, and going slower
+       * by hand was what made stages register. Between stages the sleep buys
+       * nothing, because another capture follows immediately. Keep it for the
+       * last one, where the action really is ending. */
+      self->finger_up_keep_awake = self->enroll_stage < GOODIX_ENROLL_SAMPLES;
       goodix_scan_start_finger_up_subsm (ssm, dev);
       break;
 
--- a/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-private.h
+++ b/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-private.h
@@ -255,6 +255,10 @@
   GPtrArray *enroll_features; /* array of GBytes* serialized SIGFM features */
   gint       enroll_stage;
 
+  /* Set for the finger-up wait between enrollment stages, where sleeping would
+   * cost the next stage its reference frame. Consumed by that wait. */
+  gboolean   finger_up_keep_awake;
+
   /* Consecutive no-signal reference frames in the current capture attempt. */
   guint      reference_retries;
 
--- a/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-scan.c
+++ b/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-scan.c
@@ -1034,6 +1034,15 @@
       break;
 
     case GOODIX_FINGER_UP_SLEEP:
+      /* Skipped when the caller is about to capture again. The flag is consumed
+       * here so it cannot leak into the next action, which does want the sleep. */
+      if (self->finger_up_keep_awake)
+        {
+          self->finger_up_keep_awake = FALSE;
+          fp_dbg ("Keeping the sensor awake between enrollment stages");
+          fpi_ssm_jump_to_state (ssm, GOODIX_FINGER_UP_EC_POWER_OFF);
+          return;
+        }
       goodix_cmd_set_sleep_mode (ssm, dev);
       break;
 

